{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478754-constantinople-by-night-who-survived-until-the-modern-nights","id":1478754,"title":"Constantinople By Night: Who survived until the modern nights?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-13T04:34:45-07:00","id":1478754,"title":"Constantinople By Night: Who survived until the modern nights?","content":"Paul Bathalos (DAV20) - Unknown if he survived past the Dark Ages<br /> Shabah (Survives Fourth Crusade, Dies in the Anarch Revolt)<br /> So, I am looking at setting a v5 game in Istanbul. I have always loved the concepts in Constantinople by Night, and I want to carry some of those themes and plot threads into the game. While still creating a new reality on the ground since the Ottoman seizure of the city in 1453.<br /> <br /> I have been doing some digging and I am trying to piece together what NPCs from Constantinople by Night/Bitter Crusade survived until the modern nights? Any help appreciated!<br /> <br /> Confirmed so far:<br /> <br /> <b>Mentioned in V5:</b><br /> Sascha Vykos (v5 Sabbat)<br /> The Dracon (v5 Corebook: Trinity Lore Sheet)<br /> Pakourianas The Dove (Cults of the Blood Gods)<br /> Mary the Black (v5 Corebook, Trinity Lore Sheet)<br /> Michael the Patriarch (v5 Corebook, Trinity Lore Sheet) - his consciousness is in Mary the Black<br /> <br /> <b>V20:</b><br /> Zo\u00eb (Hinted at in Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary)<br /> Sarrasine (Lore of the Clans)<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Ages</b><br /> Ana Comnena (Dark Ages Europe) Possibly returns after Ottoman Conquest<br /> Theresa Kymena - (CoBN)<br /> Enmachia (Veil of Night) Childe of Michael - flees from Damascus to Constantinople, then on to Europe<br /> Shebah (dies in the Inquistion) (CoBN)<br /> Natalya Svaytoslav (Dark Ages Europe) - possibly does not make it past the inquisition/Anarch revolt<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Revised</b><br /> Malachite (Clanbook Nosferatu Revised)<br /> <br /> <b>2nd Edition</b><br /> Abetorius, Envoy of Clan Tremere (v5 timelines, presumed dead in SI hit on Vienna, 2008)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;[Mankind] lives in a survived yet always uncertainly surviving world. All that is has survived where it might not have survived. Every world is and will always be a Noah's ark.&quot; -John Fowles, <i>The Aristos</i>","edited":{"userid":2405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2405-astriarch","user":"Astriarch","date":". 04-24-2022, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2405-astriarch","name":"Astriarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2405_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T06:13:27-07:00","id":1478756,"title":"","content":"Belisarius (he makes it into later DA books and is hinted in the Constantinople book itself that he will survive), and eventually joins the Inconnu, though it's hinted that if he ever finds out about the role they played in Constantinople's fall he may go all murder rage. So possibly he instead fell to that. There's no modern book that mentions him, but then again if he joined the Inconnu, why would there be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T06:34:24-07:00","id":1478758,"title":"","content":"Good catch on Belisarius, I completely missed that destiny bit. Baron Thomas Feroux is mentioned as joining the Inconnu as well. But, in Beckett's Jyhad Diary Vykos says that they can still taste Feroux on their tongue (or something relatively like that). So I am assuming he's dead,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;[Mankind] lives in a survived yet always uncertainly surviving world. All that is has survived where it might not have survived. Every world is and will always be a Noah's ark.&quot; -John Fowles, <i>The Aristos</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2405-astriarch","name":"Astriarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2405_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T08:06:45-07:00","id":1478764,"title":"","content":"Michael and Mary are mentioned in <b>Camarilla</b>, with &quot;Michael awakening again in Mary&quot;. They appear to be in a Mithras/Monty Coven situation, cause that's what you get for devouring a Methuselah. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T04:51:38-07:00","id":1478839,"title":"","content":"Sarrasine, a Follower of Set. Today he's the Prince of Sydney.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https:/